    "https://jobsearch.london.edu/jobs/8359110-faculty-governance-and-support-advisor": {
      "title": "Faculty Governance and Support Advisor",
      "description": "Faculty Governance and Support Advisor - London Business School Skip to main content This website uses cookies to ensure you get the best experience. London Business School and our selected partners use cookies and similar technologies (together “cookies”) that are necessary to present this website, and to ensure you get the best experience of it.\n\n          If you consent to it, we will also use cookies for analytics purposes. See our Cookie Policy to read more about the cookies we set. You can withdraw and manage your consent at any time, by clicking “Manage cookies” at the bottom of each website page. Accept all cookies Decline all non-necessary cookies Cookie preferences Select which cookies you accept On this site, we always set cookies that are strictly necessary, meaning they are necessary for the site to function properly. If you consent to it, we will also set other types of cookies. You can provide or withdraw your consent to the different types of cookies using the toggles below. You can change or withdraw your consent at any time, by clicking the link “Manage Cookies”, which is always available at the bottom of the site. To learn more about what the different types of cookies do, how your data is used when they are set etc, see our Cookie Policy . Strictly necessary These cookies are necessary to make the site work properly, and are always set when you visit the site. Vendors Teamtailor Analytics These cookies collect information to help us understand how the site is being used. Vendors Teamtailor Accept these cookies Decline all non-necessary cookies Career menu Work for us Employee Log in as employee Candidate Log in to Connect Homepage london.edu Share page Facebook X LinkedIn Mail Research and Faculty Office · London Business School, London · Hybrid Faculty Governance and Support Advisor Apply for this job Shape the future of faculty excellence. The Role At London Business School, you play a vital role in enabling world-class teaching and research. As a Faculty Governance and Support Advisor , you keep faculty operations running seamlessly — coordinating governance, managing key processes, and delivering accurate reporting that supports decision-making at the highest level. You’re organised, proactive, and confident working with senior stakeholders. You thrive in a fast-paced environment and take pride in improving processes and delivering with precision. Main Responsibilities Lead and coordinate the end-to-end faculty teaching evaluation process, ensuring accuracy and timely delivery Manage and support faculty governance and committee activity, including meetings, papers, and documentation Prepare and maintain faculty data, reports, and management information for decision-making and external requirements Coordinate faculty professional development and engagement activities, including communications and events Provide operational and administrative support across faculty-related processes and planning Act as a key point of contact for stakeholders, building relationships and ensuring clear, professional communication Who We Are Looking For Significant experience in an operational, governance, faculty support, HR administration or business support role within a complex and fast-paced organisation. Proven experience coordinating complex administrative processes involving multiple stakeholders and competing deadlines. Experience supporting committee administration, governance activity and senior stakeholder meetings. Experience preparing reports, management information and data analysis using spreadsheets and reporting systems. Experience managing or coordinating end-to-end operational processes with a high degree of accuracy and attention to detail. Experience of working collaboratively across teams and building effective relationships with senior stakeholders. Benefits You Can Enjoy Generous annual leave of 27 days plus extra days between Christmas and New Year USS pension, 14.5% employer contribution (in return for employee enrolment and contribution) Free onsite gym and swimming pool Amazing range of professional development to support your career path Enhanced cycle to work scheme Wellbeing offering to support your physical, mental and financial health At London Business School, we support Smart Working - a hybrid approach designed to help you achieve a healthy work-life balance while delivering the best outcomes for your role and the needs of our customers. All roles require a minimum of two days on campus each week to foster a vibrant, collaborative community. For this role specifically, you will be expected to be on campus 3 days per week. We operate with ‘core hours’ – 10:00-15:00 – to maximise opportunities for connection and collaboration across teams during the working day. Outside of these hours, you may still be required for meetings or collaboration based on your role and customer needs. Additionally, we offer Protected Time - a flexible, one-hour slot, within the working week dedicated to your learning and development, wellbeing, or focused, quiet work Why London Business School? London Business School; a global and vibrant business community based in three of the world’s most dynamic cities, London, Dubai and Riyadh. It’s where extraordinary minds and diverse perspectives connect, to have a profound impact on the way the world does business and the way business impacts the world. We offer best in class hybrid learning to our students and participants, whilst creating a flexible, supportive and dynamic working environment for our people to excel in, whatever their location. Our commitment to driving inclusion and belonging We are a globally reaching institution, committed to creating tangible and sustainable change in driving inclusion & belonging within our School, education and society at large. We are dedicated to creating an environment where everyone in our community feels they belong and thrive. This is a key school priority, and we want everyone who joins LBS to feel respected, welcomed, and heard. Candidates needing sponsorship should assess their eligibility for a Certificate of Sponsorship by evaluating their circumstances against the relevant criteria before applying. Please note we start screening CVs and interviewing candidates from the start of a campaign. A successful candidate could progress to offer before the advertised closing date. We encourage you to apply as soon as possible if you are interested in any roles. View Job Description View London Business School Benefits Competitive Salary dependent upon experience Closing date: Thursday 24th September 2026 Department Research and Faculty Office Locations London Business School, London Remote status Hybrid About London Business School We exist to have a profound impact on the way the world does business and the way business impacts the world. London Business School’s academic strength and global outlook drives original and provocative business thinking. We challenge conventional wisdom, transform careers and empower our people to change the way the world does business. Apply for this job Research and Faculty Office · London Business School, London · Hybrid Faculty Governance and Support Advisor Loading application form Close modal Career site Work for us Data & privacy Manage cookies london.edu/ LinkedIn Employee login Candidate Connect login Already working at London Business School? Let’s recruit together and find your next colleague. Log in Applicant tracking system by Teamtailor"
