      "title": "Associate Director, Faculty HR",
      "description": "Associate Director, Faculty HR - London Business School Skip to main content This website uses cookies to ensure you get the best experience. London Business School and our selected partners use cookies and similar technologies (together “cookies”) that are necessary to present this website, and to ensure you get the best experience of it.\n\n          If you consent to it, we will also use cookies for analytics purposes. See our Cookie Policy to read more about the cookies we set. You can withdraw and manage your consent at any time, by clicking “Manage cookies” at the bottom of each website page. Accept all cookies Decline all non-necessary cookies Cookie preferences Select which cookies you accept On this site, we always set cookies that are strictly necessary, meaning they are necessary for the site to function properly. If you consent to it, we will also set other types of cookies. You can provide or withdraw your consent to the different types of cookies using the toggles below. You can change or withdraw your consent at any time, by clicking the link “Manage Cookies”, which is always available at the bottom of the site. To learn more about what the different types of cookies do, how your data is used when they are set etc, see our Cookie Policy . Strictly necessary These cookies are necessary to make the site work properly, and are always set when you visit the site. Vendors Teamtailor Analytics These cookies collect information to help us understand how the site is being used. Vendors Teamtailor Accept these cookies Decline all non-necessary cookies Career menu Work for us Employee Log in as employee Candidate Log in to Connect Homepage london.edu Share page Facebook X LinkedIn Mail Research and Faculty Office · London Business School, London · Hybrid Associate Director, Faculty HR Apply for this job Lead Faculty HR strategy and service delivery, partnering with senior academic and professional services leaders to support excellence in teaching, research and faculty experience. The Role London Business School is looking for an experienced and collaborative Associate Director, Faculty HR to join our Research and Faculty Office. This is a senior leadership role responsible for leading the delivery of Faculty HR strategy and providing strategic and operational leadership across the full range of Faculty HR activity. You will partner with senior academic and professional services leaders to align faculty workforce planning, organisational priorities and people initiatives with the School’s strategic objectives. Reporting to the Director, RFO, you will act as a trusted adviser on complex HR matters, organisational change, policy development and governance. You will oversee activity including academic recruitment, promotion and tenure, performance and reward processes, employee relations, faculty workforce planning, budgeting, data oversight and professional development. You will also lead and develop the Faculty HR team, ensuring a high-quality, responsive and collaborative service that supports continuous improvement across faculty people processes, systems and stakeholder engagement. Main Responsibilities Lead the delivery of Faculty HR strategy, ensuring people priorities support the School’s strategic direction, RFO plans and long-term workforce requirements. Build and maintain effective relationships with senior academic leaders, School leadership teams and key stakeholders. Provide strategic HR leadership and advice on organisational priorities, workforce planning, people risks, change initiatives and faculty-related people matters. Contribute to School-wide and cross-functional initiatives, committees and projects, providing Faculty HR expertise and insight. Lead and influence discussions relating to Faculty people policy, governance and operational effectiveness. Champion change and continuous improvement by role-modelling collaborative behaviours and embedding effective people practices across faculty populations. Oversee faculty recruitment activity, ensuring effective and compliant recruitment processes, approvals and candidate engagement. Provide oversight and strategic support for faculty induction and onboarding, helping ensure a positive and effective transition into the School. Approve faculty recruitment communications, onboarding documentation and related faculty information resources. Oversee annual faculty performance review, salary review and reward-related processes, ensuring effective governance, accuracy and timely delivery. Provide senior oversight and leadership on complex employee relations matters, including cases requiring external legal support. Lead the review and continuous improvement of Faculty HR policies, processes and governance arrangements. Lead oversight of statutory, ranking and accreditation-related data submissions and reporting requirements. Lead, develop and support the Faculty HR team through effective performance management, coaching and development. Who We Are Looking For A degree, equivalent work experience or other relevant HR qualification, such as CIPD. A demonstrated track record of relationship building, persuasion and influencing. The ability to act as a resilient, driven self-starter who leads positively by example. A collaborative leadership style and the ability to role-model constructive behaviours. A solution-focused approach, strong problem-solving capability and excellent communication skills. Confidence working with ambiguity and openness to change. The ability to role-model School values, professional standards and sound judgement. A proven track record delivering people management initiatives linked to agreed plans. The ability to work naturally and purposefully across teams, including within the RFO and across the wider School. Experience advising senior stakeholders on complex HR, people policy or organisational matters. Strong understanding of HR governance, compliance and employee relations practice. Experience leading or supporting process improvement, policy development and change activity. Strong data, reporting and analytical capability to support evidence-based decision-making. Experience managing, coaching or developing a team would be advantageous. Benefits You Can Enjoy Generous annual leave of 27 days plus extra days between Christmas and New Year USS pension, 14.5% employer contribution (in return for employee enrolment and contribution) Free onsite gym and swimming pool Amazing range of professional development to support your career path Enhanced cycle to work scheme Wellbeing offering to support your physical, mental and financial health At London Business School, we support Smart Working - a hybrid approach designed to help you achieve a healthy work-life balance while delivering the best outcomes for your role and the needs of our customers. All roles require a minimum of two days on campus each week to foster a vibrant, collaborative community. For this role specifically, you will be expected to be on campus 2days per week. We operate with ‘core hours’ – 10:00-15:00 – to maximise opportunities for connection and collaboration across teams during the working day. Outside of these hours, you may still be required for meetings or collaboration based on your role and customer needs. Additionally, we offer Protected Time - a flexible, one-hour slot, within the working week dedicated to your learning and development, wellbeing, or focused, quiet work Why London Business School? London Business School; a global and vibrant business community based in three of the world’s most dynamic cities, London, Dubai and Riyadh. It’s where extraordinary minds and diverse perspectives connect, to have a profound impact on the way the world does business and the way business impacts the world. We offer best in class hybrid learning to our students and participants, whilst creating a flexible, supportive and dynamic working environment for our people to excel in, whatever their location. Our commitment to driving inclusion and belonging We are a globally reaching institution, committed to creating tangible and sustainable change in driving inclusion & belonging within our School, education and society at large. We are dedicated to creating an environment where everyone in our community feels they belong and thrive. This is a key school priority, and we want everyone who joins LBS to feel respected, welcomed, and heard. Candidates needing sponsorship should assess their eligibility for a Certificate of Sponsorship by evaluating their circumstances against the relevant criteria before applying. Please note we start screening CVs and interviewing candidates from the start of a campaign. A successful candidate could progress to offer before the advertised closing date. We encourage you to apply as soon as possible if you are interested in any roles. View Job Description View London Business School Benefits Competitive Salary dependent upon experience Closing date: 24th September 2026 Department Research and Faculty Office Locations London Business School, London Remote status Hybrid About London Business School We exist to have a profound impact on the way the world does business and the way business impacts the world. London Business School’s academic strength and global outlook drives original and provocative business thinking. We challenge conventional wisdom, transform careers and empower our people to change the way the world does business. Apply for this job Research and Faculty Office · London Business School, London · Hybrid Associate Director, Faculty HR Loading application form Close modal Career site Work for us Data & privacy Manage cookies london.edu/ LinkedIn Employee login Candidate Connect login Already working at London Business School? Let’s recruit together and find your next colleague. Log in Applicant tracking system by Teamtailor"
