    "https://jobsearch.london.edu/jobs/8449383-casual-senior-account-manager": {
      "title": "Casual Senior Account Manager",
      "description": "Casual Senior Account Manager - London Business School Skip to main content This website uses cookies to ensure you get the best experience. London Business School and our selected partners use cookies and similar technologies (together “cookies”) that are necessary to present this website, and to ensure you get the best experience of it.\n\n          If you consent to it, we will also use cookies for analytics purposes. See our Cookie Policy to read more about the cookies we set. You can withdraw and manage your consent at any time, by clicking “Manage cookies” at the bottom of each website page. Accept all cookies Decline all non-necessary cookies Cookie preferences Select which cookies you accept On this site, we always set cookies that are strictly necessary, meaning they are necessary for the site to function properly. If you consent to it, we will also set other types of cookies. You can provide or withdraw your consent to the different types of cookies using the toggles below. You can change or withdraw your consent at any time, by clicking the link “Manage Cookies”, which is always available at the bottom of the site. To learn more about what the different types of cookies do, how your data is used when they are set etc, see our Cookie Policy . Strictly necessary These cookies are necessary to make the site work properly, and are always set when you visit the site. Vendors Teamtailor Analytics These cookies collect information to help us understand how the site is being used. Vendors Teamtailor Accept these cookies Decline all non-necessary cookies Career menu Work for us Employee Log in as employee Candidate Log in to Connect Homepage london.edu Share page Facebook X LinkedIn Mail Executive Education · London Business School, London · Hybrid Casual Senior Account Manager Apply for this job Deliver world-class executive education programmes that shape leaders, strengthen client relationships in a flexible, casual role with ad hoc working hours. The Role London Business School is seeking a Senior Account Manager to join Executive Education on a casual, zero-hours contract basis for an agreed period. Working hours will be ad hoc and agreed according to business need, programme requirements and your availability. This role is central to the successful end-to-end delivery of assigned client programmes and accounts, working closely with Client Directors, Programme Directors and cross-functional teams. You will act as the primary day-to-day contact for clients, ensuring programmes are delivered to scope, budget, timeline and quality expectations. You will coordinate stakeholders, manage governance, track risks and milestones, oversee budgets and maintain a consistently high-quality client experience throughout the programme lifecycle. Executive Education designs and delivers world-class management and leadership development programmes for individuals and global client organisations. As part of this team, you will contribute directly to the School’s mission to have a profound impact on the way the world does business and the way business impacts the world. Main Responsibilities Lead the delivery of assigned custom executive education programmes, ensuring they are delivered on time, within scope and to a high standard. Act as the main day-to-day contact for clients, building strong relationships and providing clear, proactive communication. Work closely with Client Directors, Programme Directors and internal teams to coordinate programme plans, milestones, governance and resources. Manage programme risks, issues and dependencies, escalating where needed to protect delivery and client outcomes. Oversee programme budgets, financial processes and documentation, supporting commercial targets and accurate reporting. Monitor programme quality, gather feedback and support evaluation activity to drive continuous improvement. Maintain accurate client and programme records, including CRM updates and information required for reporting, planning and future business development. Who We Are Looking For We are looking for an experienced client-facing programme or account manager who can combine strong relationship management, operational delivery and commercial judgement. You will be confident working in a complex, matrixed environment and able to influence a wide range of stakeholders at all levels. This opportunity would suit someone who is comfortable working on a casual, zero-hours contract and able to provide support on an ad hoc basis, with flexibility to align availability with programme delivery requirements and business priorities. You will bring: Experience in client relationship management and key account management. Strong project or programme management experience, ideally leading project teams in a matrix environment. Excellent communication skills, with the ability to build trust and maintain effective client relationships. Proven financial management skills and strong commercial acumen. Experience in negotiation, networking and influencing. The ability to manage multiple internal and external stakeholders simultaneously. Strong judgement, attention to detail and the ability to manage risk, priorities and delivery milestones. A client-focused mindset and commitment to delivering outstanding service and continuous improvement. Flexibility to work ad hoc hours under a casual, zero-hours arrangement. Prior experience in a learning business or executive education environment would be an advantage. Working knowledge of adult learning methodologies would be an advantage. Language skills would also be an advantage. Why London Business School? London Business School; a global and vibrant business community based in three of the world’s most dynamic cities, London, Dubai and Riyadh. It’s where extraordinary minds and diverse perspectives connect, to have a profound impact on the way the world does business and the way business impacts the world. We offer best in class hybrid learning to our students and participants, whilst creating a flexible, supportive and dynamic working environment for our people to excel in, whatever their location. Our commitment to driving inclusion and belonging We are a globally reaching institution, committed to creating tangible and sustainable change in driving inclusion & belonging within our School, education and society at large. We are dedicated to creating an environment where everyone in our community feels they belong and thrive. This is a key school priority, and we want everyone who joins LBS to feel respected, welcomed, and heard. Candidates needing sponsorship should assess their eligibility for a Certificate of Sponsorship by evaluating their circumstances against the relevant criteria before applying. Please note we start screening CVs and interviewing candidates from the start of a campaign. A successful candidate could progress to offer before the advertised closing date. We encourage you to apply as soon as possible if you are interested in any roles. View Job Description Competitive Salary dependent upon experience Closing date: 8th October 2026 Department Executive Education Location London Business School, London Remote status Hybrid About London Business School We exist to have a profound impact on the way the world does business and the way business impacts the world. London Business School’s academic strength and global outlook drives original and provocative business thinking. We challenge conventional wisdom, transform careers and empower our people to change the way the world does business. Apply for this job Executive Education · London Business School, London · Hybrid Casual Senior Account Manager Loading application form Close modal Career site Work for us Data & privacy Manage cookies london.edu/ LinkedIn Employee login Candidate Connect login Already working at London Business School? Let’s recruit together and find your next colleague. Log in Applicant tracking system by Teamtailor"
    },
    "https://jobsearch.london.edu/jobs/8234391-bid-manager": {
      "title": "Bid Manager",
      "description": "Bid Manager - London Business School Skip to main content This website uses cookies to ensure you get the best experience. London Business School and our selected partners use cookies and similar technologies (together “cookies”) that are necessary to present this website, and to ensure you get the best experience of it.\n\n          If you consent to it, we will also use cookies for analytics purposes. See our Cookie Policy to read more about the cookies we set. You can withdraw and manage your consent at any time, by clicking “Manage cookies” at the bottom of each website page. Accept all cookies Decline all non-necessary cookies Cookie preferences Select which cookies you accept On this site, we always set cookies that are strictly necessary, meaning they are necessary for the site to function properly. If you consent to it, we will also set other types of cookies. You can provide or withdraw your consent to the different types of cookies using the toggles below. You can change or withdraw your consent at any time, by clicking the link “Manage Cookies”, which is always available at the bottom of the site. To learn more about what the different types of cookies do, how your data is used when they are set etc, see our Cookie Policy . Strictly necessary These cookies are necessary to make the site work properly, and are always set when you visit the site. Vendors Teamtailor Analytics These cookies collect information to help us understand how the site is being used. Vendors Teamtailor Accept these cookies Decline all non-necessary cookies Career menu Work for us Employee Log in as employee Candidate Log in to Connect Homepage london.edu Share page Facebook X LinkedIn Mail Executive Education · London Business School, London · Hybrid Bid Manager Apply for this job Turn opportunity into impact — lead winning bids for world‑class executive education. Why London Business School? London Business School; a global and vibrant business community based in three of the world’s most dynamic cities, London, Dubai and Riyadh. It’s where extraordinary minds and diverse perspectives connect, to have a profound impact on the way the world does business and the way business impacts the world. We offer best in class hybrid learning to our students and participants, whilst creating a flexible, supportive and dynamic working environment for our people to excel in, whatever their location. The Role London Business School are seeking an experienced Bid Manager to play a key role in the end‑to‑end management of bids and proposals within Executive Education. As a central stakeholder in the Bid Team, you will lead the bid process from opportunity qualification through to submission, ensuring bids are accurate, compelling, compliant and delivered on time. Working closely with sales colleagues, solution architects and commercial teams, you will shape high‑quality proposals that exceed client expectations and support the School’s growth ambitions. You will also act as a trusted advisor, sharing best practice and continuously improving bid quality and effectiveness. The Executive Education department designs and delivers a broad portfolio of open‑enrolment and custom programmes in online, in‑person and hybrid formats. Each year, more than 8,000 participants engage in our programmes, taught by leading business thinkers. Executive Education is central to the School’s strategy and generates a significant proportion of its revenue. Main Responsibilities Lead and manage the end to end bid process for qualified opportunities Qualify and scope new opportunities in partnership with senior stakeholders Ensure bids are strategically aligned, commercially viable and compliant Project manage bids to agreed timelines, quality standards and scope Work closely with sales, solution architects and commercial teams to develop winning bids Research client organisations to tailor proposals and strengthen value propositions Who We Are Looking For Proven experience in bid writing, editing and end to end bid management Strong project management skills and meticulous attention to detail Excellent written, visual and verbal communication skills Confidence working with multiple stakeholders, including senior leaders and clients Strong analytical and problem solving capability Experience using design tools such as InDesign, Illustrator, Photoshop or PowerPoint Experience in professional services, executive education or commercial learning environments (desirable) A professional bid management qualification (preferred) Benefits You Can Enjoy Generous annual leave of 27 days plus extra days between Christmas and New Year USS pension, 14.5% employer contribution (in return for employee enrolment and contribution) Free onsite gym and swimming pool Amazing range of professional development to support your career path Enhanced cycle to work scheme Wellbeing offering to support your physical, mental and financial health At London Business School, we support Smart Working - a hybrid approach designed to help you achieve a healthy work-life balance while delivering the best outcomes for your role and the needs of our customers. All roles require a minimum of two days on campus each week to foster a vibrant, collaborative community. For this role specifically, you will be expected to be on campus 2 days per week. We operate with ‘core hours’ – 10:00-15:00 – to maximise opportunities for connection and collaboration across teams during the working day. Outside of these hours, you may still be required for meetings or collaboration based on your role and customer needs. Additionally, we offer Protected Time - a flexible, one-hour slot, within the working week dedicated to your learning and development, wellbeing, or focused, quiet work Our commitment to driving inclusion and belonging We are a globally reaching institution, committed to creating tangible and sustainable change in driving inclusion & belonging within our School, education and society at large. We are dedicated to creating an environment where everyone in our community feels they belong and thrive. This is a key school priority, and we want everyone who joins LBS to feel respected, welcomed, and heard. Candidates needing sponsorship should assess their eligibility for a Certificate of Sponsorship by evaluating their circumstances against the relevant criteria before applying. Please note we start screening CVs and interviewing candidates from the start of a campaign. A successful candidate could progress to offer before the advertised closing date. We encourage you to apply as soon as possible if you are interested in any roles. View Job Description View London Business School Benefits Competitive Salary dependent upon experience Closing date: 8th October 2026 Department Executive Education Location London Business School, London Remote status Hybrid About London Business School We exist to have a profound impact on the way the world does business and the way business impacts the world. London Business School’s academic strength and global outlook drives original and provocative business thinking. We challenge conventional wisdom, transform careers and empower our people to change the way the world does business. Apply for this job Executive Education · London Business School, London · Hybrid Bid Manager Loading application form Close modal Career site Work for us Data & privacy Manage cookies london.edu/ LinkedIn Employee login Candidate Connect login Already working at London Business School? Let’s recruit together and find your next colleague. Log in Applicant tracking system by Teamtailor"
    },
    "https://jobsearch.london.edu/jobs/8205254-student-wellbeing-advisor": {
      "title": "Student Wellbeing Advisor",
      "description": "Student Wellbeing Advisor - London Business School Skip to main content This website uses cookies to ensure you get the best experience. London Business School and our selected partners use cookies and similar technologies (together “cookies”) that are necessary to present this website, and to ensure you get the best experience of it.\n\n          If you consent to it, we will also use cookies for analytics purposes. See our Cookie Policy to read more about the cookies we set. You can withdraw and manage your consent at any time, by clicking “Manage cookies” at the bottom of each website page. Accept all cookies Decline all non-necessary cookies Cookie preferences Select which cookies you accept On this site, we always set cookies that are strictly necessary, meaning they are necessary for the site to function properly. If you consent to it, we will also set other types of cookies. You can provide or withdraw your consent to the different types of cookies using the toggles below. You can change or withdraw your consent at any time, by clicking the link “Manage Cookies”, which is always available at the bottom of the site. To learn more about what the different types of cookies do, how your data is used when they are set etc, see our Cookie Policy . Strictly necessary These cookies are necessary to make the site work properly, and are always set when you visit the site. Vendors Teamtailor Analytics These cookies collect information to help us understand how the site is being used. Vendors Teamtailor Accept these cookies Decline all non-necessary cookies Career menu Work for us Employee Log in as employee Candidate Log in to Connect Homepage london.edu Share page Facebook X LinkedIn Mail Business Operations & Services · London Business School, London · Hybrid Student Wellbeing Advisor Apply for this job Maternity Leave contract until October 2027 Be part of a collaborative Wellbeing team that provides specialist, inclusive and student-centred support across a diverse and ambitious learning community. Why London Business School? London Business School; a global and vibrant business community based in three of the world’s most dynamic cities, London, Dubai and Riyadh. It’s where extraordinary minds and diverse perspectives connect, to have a profound impact on the way the world does business and the way business impacts the world. We offer best in class hybrid learning to our students and participants, whilst creating a flexible, supportive and dynamic working environment for our people to excel in, whatever their location. The Role London Business School are looking for a compassionate, knowledgeable and highly organised Student Wellbeing Advisor to support students with disabilities, mental health conditions, Specific Learning Differences and wider wellbeing needs. This is an important role within Student Wellbeing Services. You will provide professional, specialist and confidential support to students, helping them access appropriate adjustments, guidance and services so they can engage fully with their studies and academic progression. Working closely with colleagues across the School, you will support the delivery and development of student wellbeing and disability services in line with the University Mental Health Charter, the Equality Act 2010, GDPR and relevant safeguarding procedures. Main Responsibilities Provide specialist, confidential one-to-one advice and guidance to students with disabilities, mental health conditions or Specific Learning Differences. Assess students’ needs and determine suitable reasonable adjustments to support learning and academic progression. Signpost and refer students to appropriate specialist support services where required. Provide practical advice, guidance and signposting to students experiencing mental health or wellbeing challenges. Undertake initial assessments and refer students to counselling and other sources of support where necessary. Support the development, delivery and coordination of Student Wellbeing Services in line with the University Mental Health Charter and the Equality Act 2010. Liaise with the Student Association and student representatives to promote and develop wellbeing initiatives and events. Who We Are Looking For Knowledge of current principles, theory and practice relating to mental health, wellbeing, neurodivergence and disability. Experience working in higher education, disability services or wellbeing services. Understanding of student wellbeing and the needs of a diverse student population. Knowledge of the University Mental Health Charter. Experience working with Student Associations and/or student representatives. Experience handling telephone and email enquiries and working with students and staff at all levels. Experience coordinating individual support across a range of services. Strong customer-service orientation and a student-centred approach. Excellent listening, communication and stakeholder engagement skills. Excellent organisational skills, meticulous attention to detail and the ability to manage time and work autonomously. Strong IT skills, including Microsoft Office and the ability to use bespoke systems. Knowledge of relevant legislative frameworks, including the Equality Act 2010, GDPR and reasonable adjustments. Knowledge of the range of support and funding available to disabled students in higher education. Ability to identify and apply good practice and evidence from across the higher education sector to support service improvement. Benefits You Can Enjoy Generous annual leave of 27 days plus extra days between Christmas and New Year USS pension, 14.5% employer contribution (in return for employee enrolment and contribution) Free onsite gym and swimming pool Amazing range of professional development to support your career path Enhanced cycle to work scheme Wellbeing offering to support your physical, mental and financial health At London Business School, we support Smart Working - a hybrid approach designed to help you achieve a healthy work-life balance while delivering the best outcomes for your role and the needs of our customers. All roles require a minimum of two days on campus each week to foster a vibrant, collaborative community. For this role specifically, you will be expected to be on campus 3 days per week. We operate with ‘core hours’ – 10:00-15:00 – to maximise opportunities for connection and collaboration across teams during the working day. Outside of these hours, you may still be required for meetings or collaboration based on your role and customer needs. Additionally, we offer Protected Time - a flexible, one-hour slot, within the working week dedicated to your learning and development, wellbeing, or focused, quiet work Our commitment to driving inclusion and belonging We are a globally reaching institution, committed to creating tangible and sustainable change in driving inclusion & belonging within our School, education and society at large. We are dedicated to creating an environment where everyone in our community feels they belong and thrive. This is a key school priority, and we want everyone who joins LBS to feel respected, welcomed, and heard. Candidates needing sponsorship should assess their eligibility for a Certificate of Sponsorship by evaluating their circumstances against the relevant criteria before applying. Please note we start screening CVs and interviewing candidates from the start of a campaign. A successful candidate could progress to offer before the advertised closing date. We encourage you to apply as soon as possible if you are interested in any roles. View Job Description View London Business School Benefits Competitive Salary dependent upon experience Closing date: 8th October 2026 Department Business Operations & Services Location London Business School, London Remote status Hybrid About London Business School We exist to have a profound impact on the way the world does business and the way business impacts the world. London Business School’s academic strength and global outlook drives original and provocative business thinking. We challenge conventional wisdom, transform careers and empower our people to change the way the world does business. Apply for this job Business Operations & Services · London Business School, London · Hybrid Student Wellbeing Advisor Loading application form Close modal Career site Work for us Data & privacy Manage cookies london.edu/ LinkedIn Employee login Candidate Connect login Already working at London Business School? Let’s recruit together and find your next colleague. Log in Applicant tracking system by Teamtailor"
