    "https://apply.interfolio.com/193665": {
      "title": "Tenure-Track Faculty Position",
      "description": "Apply - Interfolio undefined page loaded Skip to Main Content Already have an account? Sign In Tenure-Track Faculty Position London Business School: Subject Area: Management Science and Operations Location London, UK Open Date Sep 17, 2026 Deadline Oct 15, 2026 at 11:59 PM Eastern Time Description London Business School invites applications for one tenure-track assistant professor position in Management Science & Operations starting in the 2027-28 academic year. Qualifications Applicants should hold a PhD in Management Science, Operations Research, Operations Management, Statistics or related topics by the time of appointment. In addition, applicants should have a strong research record and the ability and interest to teach Analytics and/or Operations related courses at the MBA level. London Business School is an equal opportunities employer and we particularly welcome applications from female applicants and those from ethnic minorities. Application Instructions Applicants should submit a curriculum vitae, research and teaching statements, up to three research papers, and contact information for three letters of reference by October 15. Candidates are asked in the application forms to identify two faculty members who are best able to judge their work. Questions about the application process should be emailed to Zainab Mehr at zmehr@london.edu Application Process This institution is using Interfolio's Faculty Search to conduct\n            this search. Applicants to this position receive a free Dossier\n            account and can send all application materials, including\n            confidential letters of recommendation, free of charge. Apply Now Equal Employment Opportunity Statement London Business School is an Equal Opportunities Employer. © 2026 Elsevier Inc. or its licensors and contributors. All rights are reserved, including those for text and data mining, AI training, and similar technologies. Support | Careers | Accessibility Policy 