    "https://apply.interfolio.com/127160": {
      "title": "Assistant or Associate Professor of Marketing",
      "description": "Apply - Interfolio undefined page loaded Skip to Main Content Already have an account? Sign In Assistant or Associate Professor of Marketing London Business School: Subject Area: Marketing Location London, UK Open Date Jun 20, 2023 Description London Business School is open for applications for tenure-track Assistant or Associate Professor in the Marketing subject area. While applicants from all areas of research within marketing will be considered, we have a strong preference for a quant-oriented individual. The start date for this position is expected to start in August 2024, by which time candidates are expected to have received their Ph.D. First-round interviews will take place virtually via Zoom. Research and Teaching Requirements London Business School places a strong emphasis on both research and teaching quality. Faculty are expected to publish articles in leading academic journals. Career Progression The position is tenure track. Decisions about contract renewal and promotion are based on individual performance. London Business School salaries are competitive with those at top US business schools. Environment The London Business School Marketing Faculty’s research covers a wide range of interrelated topics. Current faculty members include Jonathan Berman, Simona Botti, Rajesh Chandy, Stephanie Chen, David Faro, Dafna Goor, Bruce Hardie, Oded Koenigsberg, Anja Lambrecht, John Mullins, Nicolas Padilla, Nader Tavassoli, and Xu Zhang. London Business School is a graduate school of the University of London, and a leading centre of excellence in management education and research. It has a central location in Regent’s Park in the heart of London. The School attracts outstanding students on its MBA, Masters in Finance, Masters in Management, PhD and executive programmes. Qualifications Candidates will have a PhD, a developed area of research interest and some teaching experience. Business experience would be an advantage. For further information see http://www.london.edu/facultyandresearch/facultyrecruitment.html Application Instructions Candidates should submit (in PDF format): A cover letter Curriculum Vitae Three letters of recommendation A research statement A teaching statement At least one current research paper We will start the formal review of applications on July 3, 2023, and we highly recommend that you submit your application by 02 July at 11:59 PM Pacific Time Zone (PT). We will continue to accept applications until July 30, 2023. (Applications sent by post / courier or email will not be considered. Application Process This institution is using Interfolio's Faculty Search to conduct\n            this search. Applicants to this position receive a free Dossier\n            account and can send all application materials, including\n            confidential letters of recommendation, free of charge. Apply Now Equal Employment Opportunity Statement London Business School is an Equal Opportunities Employer. © 2026 Elsevier Inc. or its licensors and contributors. All rights are reserved, including those for text and data mining, AI training, and similar technologies. Support | Careers | Accessibility Policy | Cookies Settings | Privacy Policy | Terms of Service We use cookies that are necessary to make our site work. We may also use additional cookies to analyze, improve, and personalize our content and your digital experience. You can manage your cookie preferences using the Cookie settings link. For more information, see our Cookie Policy Cookie settings Accept all cookies Opt-Out Request Honored Cookie Preference Center We use cookies which are necessary to make our site work. We may also use additional cookies to analyse, improve and personalise our content and your digital experience. For more information, see our Cookie Policy and the list of Google Ad-Tech Vendors . You may choose not to allow some types of cookies. However, blocking some types may impact your experience of our site and the 