    "https://apply.interfolio.com/193291": {
      "title": "Apply",
      "description": "Apply - Interfolio undefined page loaded Skip to Main Content Already have an account? Sign In Affiliate Faculty positions at London Business School - OB 26/27 London Business School: Subject Area: Organisational Behaviour Location London Open Date Sep 11, 2026 Deadline Nov 01, 2026 at 11:59 PM Eastern Time Description London Business School is inviting applications for affiliate faculty to teach on the School’s master’s degree and Executive Education programmes starting in the 2027-2028 academic year. Courses may be delivered online or face-to-face, on our campuses in London or Dubai. Faculty teach in different formats, including standalone half-day or full-day sessions, 10-week courses that meet once per week or every other weekend, as well as 5-week electives. Our students range from those in our pre-experience master’s programmes (e.g., Masters in Management) to our MBA and Executive MBAs. We also offer open enrolment executive education courses. Qualifications We seek exceptional and inspirational educators, and welcome applications from people from both academic and non-academic backgrounds. Successful applicants will teach in the Organisational Behaviour Subject Area. Candidates should be able and willing to teach a selection of management and leadership courses and sessions that may include topics such as negotiations and influence, teams, leading change, power, organizational transformation, culture, innovation, personality, interpersonal dynamics, or leading in the age of AI. A PhD in a relevant field is required, and we strongly prefer candidates with evidence of successful teaching to MBA, executive, and/or early-career audiences. The ideal candidate lives in or close to London, or is willing to travel to London on their own budget. Inclusion and diversity have always been a cornerstone of London Business School’s values and we particularly welcome female applicants and those from an ethnic minority, as they are currently under-represented within our faculty. Application Instructions Please apply on Interfolio attaching your CV, a cover letter outlining your area of expertise and teaching experience, as well as representative feedback from students/participants you have previously taught. You are also strongly encouraged to submit a video sample of yourself teaching. Application Process This institution is using Interfolio's Faculty Search to conduct\n            this search. Applicants to this position receive a free Dossier\n            account and can send all application materials, including\n            confidential letters of recommendation, free of charge. Apply Now Equal Employment Opportunity Statement London Business School is an Equal Opportunities Employer. © 2026 Elsevier Inc. or its licensors and contributors. All rights are reserved, including those for text and data mining, AI training, and similar technologies. Support | Careers | Accessibility Policy | Cookies Settings | Privacy Policy | Terms of Service We use cookies that are necessary to make our site work. We may also use additional cookies to analyze, improve, and personalize our content and your digital experience. You can manage your cookie preferences using the Cookie settings link. For more information, see our Cookie Policy Cookie settings Accept all cookies Opt-Out Request Honored Cookie Preference Center We use cookies which are necessary to make our site work. We may also use additional cookies to analyse, improve and personalise our content and your digital experience. For more information, see our Cookie Policy and the list of Google Ad-Tech Vendors . You may choose not to allow some types of cookies. However, blocking some types may impact your experience of our site and the services we are able to offer. See the different category headings below to find out more or change your settings. You may also be able to exercise your privacy choices as described in our Privacy Policy Allow all Manage Consent Preference