    "https://apply.interfolio.com/190961": {
      "title": "Apply",
      "description": "Apply - Interfolio undefined page loaded Skip to Main Content Already have an account? Sign In PhD Programme in Accounting 2027 London Business School: Subject Area: Accounting PhD Location London Open Date Aug 19, 2026 Deadline Jan 06, 2027 at 11:59 PM Eastern Time Description The PhD Programme is London Business School's investment in the future of management teaching and research. Expert faculty, partnership opportunities, leading-edge research methods and close supervision contribute to an outstanding study environment. For further details please visit our website Qualifications For further details please visit our website. Application Instructions Please complete the following: 1.  Application Fee (£75) The payment should be made here: https://www.london.edu/forms/phd-payment 2. Document upload Original GMAT/GRE score report (less than five years old at the time of the application) Statement of Purpose (1000-1500 words)* Final Transcript** CV A valid original Test of English as a Foreign Language (TOEFL), International English Language Testing System (IELTS) or Duolingo score report *Statement of Purpose You should describe your reasons and motivations for pursuing a PhD in your chosen field, noting the experiences that shaped your research ambitions, indicating briefly your research interests and career objectives, and concisely stating your past research experience/work in your intended field of study. Explain why you have chosen LBS, how the faculty, research, and resources here would contribute to your future research goals. **Transcripts Transcripts for all degrees undertaken should be submitted. For applicants submitting more than one transcript or test score please use the Additional Documents tool. 3.  Two academic references 4. Forms PhD Application Form PhD Reference Form Diversity Monitoring Form Application Process This institution is using Interfolio's Faculty Search to conduct\n            this search. Applicants to this position receive a free Dossier\n            account and can send all application materials, including\n            confidential letters of recommendation, free of charge. Apply Now Equal Employment Opportunity Statement London Business School is an Equal Opportunities Employer. © 2026 Elsevier Inc. or its licensors and contributors. All rights are reserved, including those for text and data mining, AI training, and similar technologies. Support | Careers | Accessibility Policy | Cookies Settings | Privacy Policy | Terms of Service We use cookies that are necessary to make our site work. We may also use additional cookies to analyze, improve, and personalize our content and your digital experience. You can manage your cookie preferences using the Cookie settings link. For more information, see our Cookie Policy Cookie settings Accept all cookies Opt-Out Request Honored Cookie Preference Center We use cookies which are necessary to make our site work. We may also use additional cookies to analyse, improve and personalise our content and your digital experience. For more information, see our Cookie Policy and the list of Google Ad-Tech Vendors . You may choose not to allow some types of cookies. However, blocking some types may impact your experience of our site and the services we are able to offer. See the different category headings below to find out more or change your settings. You may also be able to exercise your privacy choices as described in our Privacy Policy Allow all Manage Consent Preferences Strictly Necessary Cookies Always active These cookies are necessary for the website to function and cannot be switched off in our systems. They are usually only set in response to actions made by you which amount to a request for services, such as setting your privacy preferences, logging in or filling in forms. You can set your browser to block or alert you about these cookies, but some parts of the site will not then work. Cookie Details List‎ Functional Cookies Func